# File: tests/features/add_greeting_uppercase_library_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/371-add-greeting-uppercase-library-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Upper-case the completed greeting

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Upper-case a plain greeting
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_uppercase is called with Ada, ada lovelace, and Agent 007
    Then the results are HELLO, ADA, then HELLO, ADA LOVELACE, then HELLO, AGENT 007
    And each result is a str

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Apply full Unicode upper-casing and keep uncased characters
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_uppercase is called with stra U+00DF e, U+00E9 mile, and Ada tab Bo
    Then the results are HELLO, STRASSE, then HELLO, U+00C9 MILE, then HELLO, ADA tab BO
    And each result equals greet of the same name upper-cased

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Preserve invalid-name behavior
    Given the invalid names empty, space-tab, None, and 42
    When greeting_uppercase is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Expose and document the helper
    Given the README Library section
    When the README Library example runs and prints greeting_uppercase of Ada
    Then it prints HELLO, ADA and greeting_uppercase is listed in nmg_sdlc_smoke.__all__
    And the README documents the upper-case rule and the inherited invalid-name error
